Short t-bearing fragments dominate: Persian and Turkish clues usually give
positive responses, Arabic gives negative responses, and Greek tau depends
on the preceding vowel. Separate rules cover isolated Chinese ledger/tent
and hot-water/soup characters, Indic dental t, and dot leaders. These are spelling
responses, not a general semantic detector or a full language classifier.
UTF-8 fragments and recent language clues are carried within each document.
